{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/605488-is-mummy-a-game-of-slavery","id":605488,"title":"Is Mummy a game of slavery?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-28T05:34:15-07:00","id":605488,"title":"Is Mummy a game of slavery?","content":"What the title says. I'm working on an idea for a game, where the basis of the game is that you are a slave to some one else. Part ghoul, part Promethean Tammuz, part pre-escape Changeling. And here's the question that I've got coming up - <br /> <br /> How much of Mummy do you feel is about being a slave? You're supposed to be the Judge's servant/slaves; as well, you have to obey the cult when they raise you to do stuff. How much do you feel that has an impact on the game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T05:45:02-07:00","id":605510,"title":"","content":"I'd argue it's the very core of the game. You're truly immortal, with string attached, and those strings are pulled by puppeteers. Your very memory is eroded in their service and the game's main goal, as written, is recovering your memory and breaking free of your chains. It's pretty easy to play that angle up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T06:28:53-07:00","id":605538,"title":"","content":"I've always felt the titular Curse, in fact, was not a curse laid upon interlopers, but the service to which the Arisen are bound by the Rite of Return. It's not a kind of slavery where you receive explicit orders; it's more insidious than that. It's internalized, and the path of Memory is the path of unlearning that subjugation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T10:03:13-07:00","id":605673,"title":"","content":"Power is a chain you wrap around yourself.<br /> <br /> Mummy is fundamentally about servitude, and the only &quot;freedom&quot; an Arisen can get is simply exchanging one master for another. Then there's the fact that you spend a whole lot of time cultivating servants for yourself, up to the point of eternally binding souls to your own...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 07-28-2015, 06:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T10:22:40-07:00","id":605682,"title":"","content":"It's <i>half </i>of it. An important half of it, but not the only thing in the story. Atam brought up CAS's line about power being a chain you wrap around yourself, so an immediate opposite to the slavery is power. The Arisen have a surprising amount of leeway(Just, you know, ignore morality and memory), and they sure don't look like conventional slaves. given everything they have.<br /> <br /> But, uh, yeah. Mummy is very much a game about slavery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T13:26:54-07:00","id":605891,"title":"","content":"The basic truth of the setting is that if you're a mummy - Arisen, Deceived or Shuankhsen - you're not your own free man. Someone (who that someone is differs between factions) is playing puppetmaster and using you as a slave/tool/soldier in its war. And we're talking about a war that is most likely significantly older than 6000 years, and that has most likely lost all meaning in the context of the present time. The tragedy of the setting is that mummies are slaves; to causes that have died millenia ago. <br /> <br /> At its core, Mummy is a game about exploring social themes in the context of what has and has not changed in the last 6000 years. Mummy is about about slavery, and the underclasses of the world, about the people who suffer so that the privileged get to enjoy a nice life. <br /> <br /> To quote one of the authors of the game: <br /> <br /> &quot;Workers, not Kings. The Arisen see modern, Western, people claim that they're better than their ancestors, that their Empire frees people, and they see prison workforces and starving factory workers.<br /> <br /> The decline of the Old Kingdom. The fall of the New Kingdom. The end of Christian rule. 2012.<br /> <br /> The Arisen see your Empires, and they are not impressed.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T13:27:18-07:00","id":605892,"title":"","content":"Yes. A mummy is a slave. Now what is the mummy going to do about it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-28T15:45:26-07:00","id":606016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/605488-is-mummy-a-game-of-slavery?p=605673#post605673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mummy is fundamentally about servitude, and the only &quot;freedom&quot; an Arisen can get is simply exchanging one master for another.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're confusing Deceived and Arisen there. Arisen can most certainly win freedom and become their own masters. It is the Deceived who are unable to ever become truly free.<br /> <br /> On topic though, yes, as others have been saying, it's absolutely a game about slavery. There's a strong old age/dementia metaphor underlying the game's primary interlinked mechanics of Sekhem and Memory, but even they feed it into the game's slavery themes. You have the choice to sacrifice your identity to please your master and cling to power for just a little while longer, while attempting to restore your sense of self and reclaim your history has the side-effect of sending you spiralling down your Descent a whole lot faster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T01:08:03-07:00","id":607553,"title":"","content":"Yes, so?<br /> <br /> As others have mentioned; that is not full story. It should be stressed that it does not glorify slavery, it does not shy away from the harshness of it or force you to remain a slave. You could even have been willing at first; an eternity serving the will of your divine Lord might not have seemed like a bad deal at the time. I imagine there are a lot of people today in the western world who would jump at such a chance if they believed it was genuine.<br /> <br /> But in Mummy you also are old, tired and weary. The world you wake too has it's own magic, it's own laws even it's own language. You've seen things, done thing; things you can't even remember and coming to question the very thing you've devoted your immortal life towards. Your 'owner' is not a close one and there is rumours that you can slip the leash. But it was your god, something you served for longer than you can remember...<br /> Over the years, you've amassed power and influence but the strength to summon miracles fades with each breath and with it goes your waking hours. So do you use it to serve yourself and live your life or do you do the master's bidding? A bit of both, perhaps?<br /> <br /> And that is the standard set-up, the vanillia setting, the basic assumption made in the corebook. It has other, equally interesting frameworks in the corebook, yes (I would love to run a pyramid style game), but the general idea is that you play one of the Arisen. Slavery isn't the point, anymore than indentured servitude is the point in Vampire the Masquerade. It does that very well, but it is a tool to drive the story, not a straight-jacket to railroad you.<br /> <br /> You don't have to stay a slave or even see the position of your kind as slaves. But you are called to serve, to act in certain ways. What you choose to do with that is the intriguing part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T04:54:41-07:00","id":607663,"title":"","content":"Hmm.... so, while Slavery is a thing, its sounding much more diluted than what I'm looking for. <br /> <br /> Thanks all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}